-id=` + `\"` + `12345` + `\"` + `[^>]+` = ` ` + `data-quality=`. Good. media_id = '12345'.\n\nsources findall: `<button[^>]+data-quality=([\"\\'])(.+?)\\1` \u2014 for button 1: `data-quality=\"360\"` \u2192 ('\"', '360'). Button 2: ('\"', '720'). sources = ['360', '720']. \n\nNote: `.+?` with no DOTALL \u2014 fine, single line.\n\nNow `if not (media_id and sources)` \u2192 media_id='12345', sources non-empty \u2192 False \u2192 skip lines 87-97. \n\n`formats = self._extract_formats(url, video_id, media_id, sources)` \u2014 url here is the (possibly rewritten) url. In test 1, url unchanged.\n\nReturn dict \u2014 all keys as asserted above.\n\nNow FALLBACK_WEBPAGE:\n\n```python\nFALLBACK_WEBPAGE = r'''\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta name=\"name\" content=\"Fallback Video Title\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"player\">\n<script id='playerembed' src='https://static.example.com/player.js'></script>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n'''\n```\n\nCheck: `_html_search_meta('name', ...)` \u2192 'Fallback Video Title'. uploadDate \u2192 None \u2192 timestamp None. thumbnailUrl \u2192 None. uploader regexes \u2192 None. categories \u2192 None \u2192 categories None. view/like \u2192 None. duration \u2192 None. media_id \u2192 None (no buttons). sources \u2192 []. \u2192 fallback.\n\nPlayer JS regex on FALLBACK_WEBPAGE: `<script[^>]id=([\"\\'])playerembed\\1[^>]+src=([\"\\'])(?P<url>.+?)\\2`. \n\n`<script` then `[^>]` \u2014 the next char is ` ` (space) \u2014 matches. Then `id=` \u2014 matches. Then `'` `playerembed` `'`. Then `[^>]+` \u2014 ` ` \u2014 then `src=` \u2014 then `'` \u2014 then `(?P<url>.+?)` \u2014 non-greedy \u2014 `https://static.example.com/player.js` \u2014 then `\\2` = `'`. Good. url = 'https://static.example.com/player.js'.\n\nHmm wait \u2014 `.+?` non-greedy followed by `'` \u2014 the URL contains no quote, so it matches up to the first `'` after src. Good.\n\nPLAYER_JS:\n\n```python\nPLAYER_JS = r'''\n(function(global) {\n  function init() {\n    $.ajax(url, opts);\n  }\n })(12345, 0, [360, 720]);\n})();\n'''\n```\n\nCheck regex: `\\$\\.ajax\\(url,\\ opts\\);\\s*\\}\\s*\\}\\)\\(([0-9,\\[\\] ]+)\\)`.\n\n- `$.ajax(url, opts);` \u2014 matches literally.\n- `\\s*` \u2014 `\\n  ` (whitespace before `}`).\n- `\\}` \u2014 `}`.\n- `\\s*` \u2014 `\\n `.\n- `\\}\\)\\(` \u2014 `})(`.\n- `([0-9,\\[\\] ]+)` \u2014 `12345, 0, [360, 720]`.\n- `\\)` \u2014 `)`.\n\nGood. params_js = '12345, 0, [360, 720]'. `'[12345, 0, [360, 720]]'` \u2192 json \u2192 [12345, 0, [360, 720]]. params[0] = 12345. params[2] = [360, 720] \u2192 sources = ['360', '720'].\n\nWait \u2014 `self._parse_json('[%s]' % params_js, video_id)` \u2014 parse_json with default strict mode. json.loads('[12345, 0, [360, 720]]') \u2192 fine.\n\nHmm, but `_parse_json` signature: `_parse_json(self, json_string, video_id, transform_source=None, fatal=True, ...)`. Called with two args. Fine.\n\nNow \u2014 in the fallback test, `_download_webpage` is called twice. My fake pops from a list: [FALLBACK_WEBPAGE, PLAYER_JS]. Assert downloaded == [(video_url, '99999'), ('https://static.example.com/player.js', '99999')].\n\nAnd `_extract_formats` called with (url_after_rewrite, '99999', 12345, ['360', '720']). Note: if the fallback test URL has no display_id, url gets rewritten to template. Let me use a URL with display_id and kind != 'm' so url stays the input: `https://www.fourtube.com/videos/99999/fallback-title`. Then url unchanged.\n\nHmm wait \u2014 but does the real FourTubeIE._VALID_URL support 'www' kind? If the pattern is `(?:(?P<kind>www|m)\\.)?` then 'www' matches kind='www'. If the pattern is `(?:www\\.)?` without kind group... then 'kind' group must exist somewhere else. get_info will clarify.\n\nNow the timestamp: I'll compute expected via calendar.timegm((2016, 5, 7, 12, 34, 56)) if the format is 'Z'-suffixed UTC. But if parse_iso8601 in this version doesn't handle 'Z'... Let me check. Actually the youtube_dl parse_iso8601 (modern):\n\n```python\ndef parse_iso8601(date_str, timez