0\">360p</button>\n<button data-id=\"12345\" data-quality=\"720\">720p</button>\n</body>\n</html>\n'''\n```\n\nWait, there's an issue with the categories regex and the `<ul>`: `.*?<ul class=\"[^\"]*?list[^\"]*?\">` \u2014 my `<ul class=\"list-tags\">` \u2014 `[^\"]*?` lazy matches empty, then `list` matches 'list', then `[^\"]*?` matches '-tags', then `\">`. Good.\n\nBut hold on \u2014 the regex `(?s)><i class=\"icon icon-tag\"></i>\\s*Categories / Tags\\s*.*?<ul class=\"[^\"]*?list[^\"]*?\">(.*?)</ul>` \u2014 the `.*?` between `Tags\\s*` and `<ul` \u2014 with DOTALL, non-greedy. Between `Categories / Tags\\n` and `<ul class=...` there's just `\\n`. Good.\n\nCapture `(.*?)</ul>` \u2192 `\\n<li><a href=\"/tag/one\"> One </a></li>\\n<li><a href=\"/tag/two\">Two</a></li>\\n`. findall `<li><a.*?>(.*?)</a>` \u2192 [' One ', 'Two'] \u2192 ['One', 'Two']. \n\nNow the uploader regex \u2014 check the `title=\"Go to [^\"]+ page\">` part: my anchor has `title=\"Go to Uploader One page\">Subscribe</a>`. After `page\">` the regex ends. Good.\n\nHmm wait, one thing: the regex for uploader_id: `href=\"[^\"]+/(?:channel|user)s?/([^/\"]+)\"`. My href: `https://www.fourtube.com/channel/uploader1`. `[^\"]+` greedy: tries `https://www.fourtube.com/channel/uploader1` then `/`? No more `/` before `\"`. Backtrack: `[^\"]+` = `https://www.fourtube.com/channel/uploader1` minus... let's find positions where `/(?:channel|user)s?/` can match after `[^\"]+`. The string: `https://www.fourtube.com/channel/uploader1`. Possible: `[^\"]+` = `https://www.fourtube.com`, then `/channel/` matches, then `([^/\"]+)` = `uploader1`, then `\"` \u2014 yes. Also `[^\"]+` = `https://www.fourtube.com/channel/uploader` then... `/` then `(?:channel|user)` \u2014 next chars after `uploader` are `1\"` \u2014 no. So unique match. Good.\n\nNow the media_id regex: `<button[^>]+data-id=([\"\\'])(?P<id>\\d+)\\1[^>]+data-quality=`. My button: `<button data-id=\"12345\" data-quality=\"360\">`. `<button` + `[^>]+` = ` ` + `data-id=` + `\"` + `12345` + `\"` + `[^>]+` = ` ` + `data-quality=`. Good. media_id = '12345'.\n\nsources findall: `<button[^>]+data-quality=([\"\\'])(.+?)\\1` \u2014 for button 1: `data-quality=\"360\"` \u2192 ('\"', '360'). Button 2: ('\"', '720'). sources = ['360', '720']. \n\nNote: `.+?` with no DOTALL \u2014 fine, single line.\n\nNow `if not (media_id and sources)` \u2192 media_id='12345', sources non-empty \u2192 False \u2192 skip lines 87-97. \n\n`formats = self._extract_formats(url, video_id, media_id, sources)` \u2014 url here is the (possibly rewritten) url. In test 1, url unchanged.\n\nReturn dict \u2014 all keys as asserted above.\n\nNow FALLBACK_WEBPAGE:\n\n```python\nFALLBACK_WEBPAGE = r'''\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta name=\"name\" content=\"Fallback Video Title\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"player\">\n<script id='playerembed' src='https://static.example.com/player.js'></script>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n'''\n```\n\nCheck: `_html_search_meta('name', ...)` \u2192 'Fallback Video Title'. uploadDate \u2192 None \u2192 timestamp None. thumbnailUrl \u2192 None. uploader regexes \u2192 None. categories \u2192 None \u2192 categories None. view/like \u2192 None. duration \u2192 None. media_id \u2192 None (no buttons). sources \u2192 []. \u2192 fallback.\n\nPlayer JS regex on FALLBACK_WEBPAGE: `<script[^>]id=([\"\\'])playerembed\\1[^>]+src=([\"\\'])(?P<url>.+?)\\2`. \n\n`<script` then `[^>]` \u2014 the next char is ` ` (space) \u2014 matches. Then `id=` \u2014 matches. Then `'` `playerembed` `'`. Then `[^>]+` \u2014 ` ` \u2014 then `src=` \u2014 then `'` \u2014 then `(?P<url>.+?)` \u2014 non-greedy \u2014 `https://static.example.com/player.js` \u2014 then `\\2` = `'`. Good. url = 'https://static.example.com/player.js'.\n\nHmm wait \u2014 `.+?` non-greedy followed by `'` \u2014 the URL contains no quote, so it matches up to the first `'` after src. Good.\n\nPLAYER_JS:\n\n```python\nPLAYER_JS = r'''\n(function(global) {\n  function init() {\n    $.ajax(url, opts)