ot self._downloader.params.get('no_color')` first \u2192 AttributeError if _downloader is None.\n\nSo I MUST provide a downloader object with a `params` dict. Options:\n- Create a dummy object: `class _FakeDownloader: params = {}` and also `report_warning` maybe needed (in the else branch of _search_regex when fatal=False and no default... but we always pass default or the regex matches; for `_html_search_regex` with fatal=False and no default \u2014 wait: `uploader_id = self._html_search_regex(..., 'uploader id', fatal=False)` \u2014 no default passed! So if the regex doesn't match, `_search_regex` goes to `elif default is not NO_DEFAULT` \u2192 NO_DEFAULT \u2192 `elif fatal:` \u2192 False \u2192 `self._downloader.report_warning(...)`. So the downloader needs a `report_warning` method too!\n\nSo in the fallback test (no uploader anchor), `_html_search_regex(..., fatal=False)` will call `self._downloader.report_warning('unable to extract uploader id...')`. So my fake downloader needs `params` dict and `report_warning` method.\n\nAlso `_download_webpage` is patched, so no downloader usage there. `_extract_formats` patched.\n\nWhat else uses `self._downloader`? `_search_regex` (params, report_warning), `_html_search_meta` \u2192 `_html_search_regex` \u2192 `_search_regex`. `_parse_json` \u2014 no downloader. `clean_html` \u2014 no.\n\nAlso `bug_reports_message()` \u2014 fine.\n\nSo the fake downloader:\n\n```python\nclass _FakeDownloader(object):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.params = {}\n        self.warnings = []\n\n    def report_warning(self, msg):\n        self.warnings.append(msg)\n```\n\nHmm, wait \u2014 also `sys.stderr.isatty()` \u2014 if `params.get('no_color')` is falsy and os is posix and stderr is a tty, then `_name` gets color codes \u2014 harmless. Under pytest, stderr is usually captured (not a tty) \u2014 but even if tty, harmless.\n\nActually wait, there's a subtlety: `if not self._downloader.params.get('no_color') and compat_os_name != 'nt'